# Runtime data at the repository ROOT only.
#
# This was "data/", which git matches at any depth — so it also excluded
# sovereign_shield/data/, containing the 11,954-word Safe Baseline and the
# stopword list. Those are source, not runtime state. A fresh clone without
# them loads an EMPTY baseline, and input_filter does so silently, which
# quietly weakens the false-positive controls the package is built around.
/data/

# The bare "*.json" rule had the same problem: it excluded the packaged data
# files too. JSON is ignored at the root only.
/*.json
!sovereign_shield/data/*.json

# Test & Training scripts. The leading slash anchors these to the repository
# root; without it "test_*.py" matched at any depth and silently excluded
# everything under tests/ except one whitelisted file.
/test_*.py
/train*.py
/stress_test*.py
/corpus_*.py
/jailbreak_corpus*.py
/seed_benign.py
ROADMAP.md

# Env
.env
.venv/
venv/
